window.DOCS_INDEX=[{"p":"Quick Start","h":"Quick Start","u":"getting-started.html#quick-start","x":"Your first working door in about five minutes. No code. Drag in your prefab, check what the wizard found, press Play."},{"p":"Quick Start","h":"1. Try the demo (1 minute)","u":"getting-started.html#1-try-the-demo-1-minute","x":"Open Samples/Scenes/InteractionKit_Demo3D and press Play . Walk with WASD , look with the mouse, and press E (or X / Square on a controller) at a door. Things to try: the Physics Door : walk into it and it swings open; the Locked Door : pick up the red key first; the Hold Door : hold the button until the ring fills; behind you: cabinets, drawers, a bookcase and a fridge, all made with the Setup Wizard."},{"p":"Quick Start","h":"2. Make your own model interactive (2 minutes)","u":"getting-started.html#2-make-your-own-model-interactive-2-minutes","x":"Tools > All In One Interaction Kit > Setup Wizard . Drag your prefab or model into Prefab . - Furniture with doors or drawers as separate child objects (named like door , lid or drawer ): the wizard lists each moving part . Check the type and hinge side of each. - A single door: pick the Hinge side . The wizard tells you if the pivot is in the middle (it will fix that). Click Create Interactive Prefab . A new prefab appears next to your original; your original is never changed."},{"p":"Quick Start","h":"3. Set up the player (2 minutes)","u":"getting-started.html#3-set-up-the-player-2-minutes","x":"On your player (or the demo's Player prefab as a reference), add: Interactor , and set its Origin to your camera. Look Ray Discovery (first person) or Proximity Discovery (third person, top-down). Key Interaction Input (E key and a gamepad button). With the Input System package you can use Input Action Interaction Input instead. Add an empty GameObject to the scene with Interaction Prompt (No Packages) and, for first person, Interaction Crosshair . Drag your new prefab into the scene, press Play , look at it and press E ."},{"p":"Quick Start","h":"Something not working?","u":"getting-started.html#something-not-working","x":"Add an Interaction Debug Overlay to the scene and press F3 in Play mode: it shows what the player is looking at and exactly why it can't be used. More in Troubleshooting ."},{"p":"Setup Wizard","h":"Setup Wizard","u":"setup-wizard.html#setup-wizard","x":"Tools > All In One Interaction Kit > Setup Wizard , or right-click a prefab in the Project window > All In One Interaction Kit > Make Interactive Door . The wizard never edits your prefab or model. It saves a new prefab next to it ( <Name>_Interactive.prefab ) that contains your original as a nested prefab, so later changes to your original still show up."},{"p":"Setup Wizard","h":"Picking your prefab","u":"setup-wizard.html#picking-your-prefab","x":"Any of these works: click a prefab in the Project window while the wizard is open: it picks it up straight away; drag it onto the Prefab field, or use the field's circle to browse; select an instance of it in your scene (Hierarchy or Scene view) and press Use selected : the wizard uses the prefab it comes from; a scene object that isn't a prefab yet: press Save as prefab and use it ."},{"p":"Setup Wizard","h":"The preview","u":"setup-wizard.html#the-preview","x":"With Preview in Scene view on, a copy of your prefab appears where the Scene view is looking. For every moving part it shows: a yellow box around the part; hinged parts: the hinge line , and an arc for how far it opens and which way (blue: outward, orange: the other way for doors that open either way), with a label such as Door: left hinge, opens 100°, outward ; drawers: an arrow and an outline where the drawer ends up, labelled with how far it slides. Change a value in the wizard and the preview follows. The copy is never saved with your scene and goes when the wizard closes."},{"p":"Setup Wizard","h":"Models with moving parts","u":"setup-wizard.html#models-with-moving-parts","x":"The wizard finds a model's moving parts: by name : child objects named like door , lid , hatch , gate , flap , drawer or tray ; by shape , when nothing is named like that (children called Cube , Cube (1) ...): thin panels on the front of the model become doors, boxes set into the front become drawers. Handles and knobs are too small to count, and the biggest piece is the body. These are marked guessed from its shape : check them in the preview. Not right? Change a part's type, remove it (x), or add one: click a part of the preview in the Scene view or the Hierarchy (or pick it from the Part li"},{"p":"Setup Wizard","h":"Single objects","u":"setup-wizard.html#single-objects","x":"A prefab without moving parts becomes what you pick as Type : Door : swings on a hinge (below); Switch : on/off; Button : springs back after a press; Lever : tilts forward around its base. All three can power things (see Power and puzzles ); Pressure Plate : powers things while weight stands on it; the detection box covers the model and half a metre above; Container : a crate to search for loot; Carryable , Inspectable , Readable , Keypad , Item Socket : see Carry, sockets, inspect, notes and keypads ."},{"p":"Setup Wizard","h":"Single doors","u":"setup-wizard.html#single-doors","x":"For a door, the wizard measures where the pivot is: pivot in the middle (common for store models): it adds a hinge pivot on the edge you choose; pivot already on an edge : it still wraps the door so your original stays untouched. Pick the Hinge side , Opens (degrees) , Swing and Motion , then Create Interactive Prefab . Doors default to Away From Player : they open away from whoever opens them, from either side."},{"p":"Setup Wizard","h":"After creating","u":"setup-wizard.html#after-creating","x":"Drag the prefab into a scene and select the door: the Hinge inspector has a Preview slider and Closed , Open and Other way buttons, and the Scene view shows the arcs and a handle you can drag to set the open angle. Nothing in the preview is saved."},{"p":"Setup Wizard","h":"Tips","u":"setup-wizard.html#tips","x":"Name your parts clearly in your 3D app ( door , drawer ): the wizard finds them by name. Unnamed parts are guessed from their shape, and you can always add or change parts by clicking them. To make a door open one way only, set Swing on its Hinge to Outward Only or Inward Only . Physics doors ignore collisions with the rest of their own model (the frame or cabinet body) so they never jam."},{"p":"Samples","h":"Samples","u":"samples.html#samples","x":"All in Samples/Scenes . They use only what ships with the kit and look the same in Built-in, URP and HDRP. Scene What it shows InteractionKit_Demo3D First person: a smooth door, a physics door you can walk into, a locked door with a key, a hold-to-open door, a row of furniture (cabinets, drawers, bookcase, fridge) made with the Setup Wizard, a Make it yours button that switches the prompt, crosshair and highlight between the ready-made themes, and a More objects corner to your left: a valve that lights a lamp when fully turned (press it, or hold E and drag it), a crate that breaks, a chair to "},{"p":"Components","h":"Components","u":"components.html#components","x":"Every component is under Add Component > All In One Interaction Kit . Hover any setting in the Inspector for a tooltip."},{"p":"Components","h":"On the player","u":"components.html#on-the-player","x":""},{"p":"Components","h":"Interactor","u":"components.html#interactor","x":"Finds what the player can use and sends the interact button to it. Discovery : how it finds things (below). Empty = the one on the same GameObject. Input : the interact button (below). Empty = the one on the same GameObject. Origin : where rays and distances are measured from, usually the camera."},{"p":"Components","h":"Discovery","u":"components.html#discovery","x":"Look Ray Discovery : what the camera points at (first person). Radius above 0 makes small objects easier to hit. Proximity Discovery : the best object near the player (third person, top-down). Prefers what is in front. Proximity 2D Discovery : the same for 2D games (2D colliders)."},{"p":"Components","h":"Input","u":"components.html#input","x":"Key Interaction Input : a keyboard key (default E ) and a gamepad button (default the left face button: X on Xbox, Square on PlayStation, Y on Switch). Works with the old Input Manager and the Input System package. Input Action Interaction Input (Input System package only): any Input Action, so players can rebind it."},{"p":"Components","h":"Key Ring","u":"components.html#key-ring","x":"The keys the player carries (just names, like red ). Locks check it; key pickups add to it."},{"p":"Components","h":"On the objects","u":"components.html#on-the-objects","x":""},{"p":"Components","h":"Interactable","u":"components.html#interactable","x":"Makes an object usable. Every interactable object has one. Display Name : shown in the prompt (\"Open Door \"). Prompt Override : your own prompt text instead of \" \". Max Distance : how close the player must be. Priority : wins when several objects are in reach. Mode : Press , or Hold for Hold Duration seconds (the prompt shows a ring that fills). Cooldown : minimum time between uses. Max Concurrent Users : how many players may hold it at once (0 = unlimited). Events : On Interacted , On Denied , On Hold Started , On Hold Canceled , On State Changed : hook up sounds, animations or your own scrip"},{"p":"Components","h":"Hinge (doors, lids, gates, levers)","u":"components.html#hinge-doors-lids-gates-levers","x":"Rotates a Pivot between Closed Angle and Open Angle around Local Axis . Hinge Point lets a part turn around its edge when its pivot is in the middle. Start Open , Block While Moving , and the Open / Close verbs for the prompt. Swing sets which way it opens: Away From Player (the default for doors): either way, always away from the player who opens or walks into it. In multiplayer the host decides from that player's position, and the side is part of the saved and synced state. Outward Only : always to the Open Angle . Use it for furniture doors, lids and levers, which can only open one way. Inw"},{"p":"Components","h":"Slide (drawers, sliding doors, trays)","u":"components.html#slide-drawers-sliding-doors-trays","x":"Moves a Target along Direction by Distance , smoothly over Duration . Start Open , Block While Moving , and the prompt verbs."},{"p":"Components","h":"Switch","u":"components.html#switch","x":"An on/off switch (\"Turn On\" / \"Turn Off\") or, in Momentary mode, a push button (\"Press\"). Can power things: see Power and puzzles , which also covers Pressure Plate, Power Gate, Sequence Puzzle, Power Receiver, Needs Power and Powered Light."},{"p":"Components","h":"Carry, Item Socket, Inspect, Readable, Keypad","u":"components.html#carry-item-socket-inspect-readable-keypad","x":"Pick up and throw, place items, look at things up close, read notes, enter codes. See Carry, sockets, inspect, notes and keypads ."},{"p":"Components","h":"Loot Container","u":"components.html#loot-container","x":"Hands out items when used. See Containers and loot ."},{"p":"Components","h":"Key Pickup","u":"components.html#key-pickup","x":"Gives a key name to the player's Key Ring and hides the object (\"Take Red Key\")."},{"p":"Components","h":"Lock","u":"components.html#lock","x":"Blocks the object until the player has the key named in Key Id . Locked Message is the reason shown in the prompt. Consume Key removes the key when used."},{"p":"Components","h":"Interaction Sounds","u":"components.html#interaction-sounds","x":"Your AudioClips for the object: Opened / Closed (every player hears them), Used , Denied , and slots for keypads, carrying and loot. See Customizing ."},{"p":"Components","h":"In the scene","u":"components.html#in-the-scene","x":"Interaction Prompt (No Packages) : the on-screen prompt. Needs nothing else. See Prompts . Interaction Prompt (uGUI) : the same with a Canvas and TextMesh Pro (when your project has uGUI). Interaction Crosshair : a small dot that lights up on usable objects and turns red when something is blocked. Interaction Debug Overlay : press F3 in Play mode to see why something can't be used. A development aid; leave it out of release builds."},{"p":"Components","h":"More components","u":"components.html#more-components","x":"The feature pass added many more; each has its own page: Ways to interact : Interaction Actions, Drag Interaction, Auto Interact Zone, Gaze Interaction Input, Pointer Discovery, Pointer Interaction Input, Interaction Touch Button, Interaction Rebinding, Interaction Highlighter, Interaction Markers and Interaction Marker. More ready-made objects : Item Pickup, Valve Or Wheel, Combination Dial, Ladder, Seat, Sign, Audio Log, Breakable, Screen, Linked Parts, Roll-Up Door, Elevator Or Moving Platform, Elevator Call Button, Use Limit, Custom Condition, Auto Reset, Camera Focus Point, Play Director "},{"p":"Ways to interact","h":"Ways to interact","u":"ways-to-interact.html#ways-to-interact","x":"Every way a player can find and use objects, and how to switch each one on. Everything here works with both input systems, keyboard, mouse, gamepad and touch, and costs no garbage per frame."},{"p":"Ways to interact","h":"How an object is used","u":"ways-to-interact.html#how-an-object-is-used","x":"Set Mode on the object's Interactable : Mode The player... Settings Press presses the button once Hold keeps the button down until the ring fills Hold Duration Double Tap presses twice quickly Tap Window Mash presses again and again (a stuck door, a winch) Mash Count, Tap Window (the count drains when they slow down) The prompt says how (\"Hold to Open Door\", \"Double-tap to Open Door\", \"Tap repeatedly to Force Door\"); change those words on the prompt (Hold Format, Double Tap Format, Mash Format). Players can turn Mash into Hold and Double Tap into Press, and holds into toggles, in the accessibi"},{"p":"Ways to interact","h":"Several actions on one object","u":"ways-to-interact.html#several-actions-on-one-object","x":"Add Interaction Actions (Several Per Object) next to the Interactable. Each action has a verb, how it is triggered and what it runs (one of the object's parts, an event, or both): Press and Hold on the same button: tap to open, hold to lock. A tap is letting go within Tap Time. Own Key : its own key and gamepad button (F to kick, Q to knock). Menu Only : only in the radial menu. Menu: Stacked lists the extra actions under the prompt, each as a small prompt of its own with its key cap (\"[F] Kick\", \"[E] Hold to Lock\"). Menu: Radial opens a ring of all actions when the player holds the button: th"},{"p":"Ways to interact","h":"Grab and move by hand","u":"ways-to-interact.html#grab-and-move-by-hand","x":"Add Drag Interaction (Grab And Move) to a door, drawer, lever, valve or wheel. Players hold the button on it and move the mouse (or the right stick) to swing it, pull it or turn it, as far as they like; when they let go it settles open or closed. A quick tap still opens and closes it as usual. Physics doors keep their swing. Set the speed per object (Degrees Per Pixel, Metres Per Pixel) and flip the direction with Invert."},{"p":"Ways to interact","h":"Without pressing anything","u":"ways-to-interact.html#without-pressing-anything","x":"Auto Interact Zone : a trigger area that uses objects when a player walks in (automatic doors, pickups you walk over) and optionally when they leave (close the gate behind them). Can be limited to players who turned on Auto Interact in the accessibility settings. Gaze Interaction Input : looking at an object for a moment uses it (Dwell Time). Set it as the Interactor's input and give it your key input as Also Use, so both work. Its On Progress event drives a filling ring."},{"p":"Ways to interact","h":"Mouse, touch and phones","u":"ways-to-interact.html#mouse-touch-and-phones","x":"Pointer Discovery (Mouse And Touch) finds the object under the mouse, or under the finger that tapped it (touch screens have no hover, so a tapped object stays picked for a few seconds). 3D and 2D. Pointer Interaction Input (Click And Tap) : clicking or tapping the object uses it; holding works for Hold objects. Interaction Touch Button : an on-screen button for phones that shows the action (\"Open\") and works as the interact button. Shown on touch devices only by default. Call Pointer Down / Pointer Up from your own UI button instead if you like. On a touch screen the prompt says \"Tap to Open "},{"p":"Ways to interact","h":"Rebinding","u":"ways-to-interact.html#rebinding","x":"Key Interaction Input : call Listen For Key from your settings menu; the next key or gamepad button becomes the interact button (Escape cancels). Set Remember Binding As to keep it between sessions. Interaction Rebinding (Input System) : rebinds the interact action's keyboard or gamepad binding, saves it, and can reset it. Prompts show the new button at once."},{"p":"Ways to interact","h":"Finding what the player means","u":"ways-to-interact.html#finding-what-the-player-means","x":"Look Ray Discovery : a ray from the camera. Cone Angle adds aim assist: when the ray just misses, the best object within that angle is picked (never through walls). Angle Weight decides how much being off centre counts. Proximity Discovery (third person, top-down): the nearest object around the player. Max Angle limits it to what is in front; Require Line Of Sight skips objects behind walls. The 2D version has line of sight too. Sticky Focus Time on the Interactor keeps the current object a moment longer, so the prompt doesn't flicker at the edge of range."},{"p":"Ways to interact","h":"Seeing what can be used","u":"ways-to-interact.html#seeing-what-can-be-used","x":"Interaction Highlighter : marks the object being looked at with an outline, a tint, a rim glow, a pulse, or nothing, in Built-in, URP and HDRP, without touching your materials. The look comes from the theme (each preset has one) or a Highlight Style asset; objects that can't be used get the blocked colour. An Interaction Appearance turns it off for one object. Interaction Markers (Nearby And Off Screen) : a dot or icon over each usable object near the player, fading with distance, and arrows at the edge of the screen to important objects that are off screen. An Interaction Marker on an object "},{"p":"More ready-made objects","h":"More ready-made objects","u":"more-objects.html#more-ready-made-objects","x":"Each of these is a component you add next to an Interactable (or the Setup Wizard adds for you). All of them save their state (see Saving ), work in multiplayer, and have events for your own effects."},{"p":"More ready-made objects","h":"Things to pick up","u":"more-objects.html#things-to-pick-up","x":"Item Pickup : an item lying in the world. Kind To Inventory hands it to the player's inventory through your Loot Receiver (keys go to the Key Ring), Consume uses it on the spot (On Consumed: heal, add ammo), Collectible counts it (On Collected, and a static Collected event for \"3 / 10 found\"). It can respawn after a while. When the inventory is full it stays and says \"No room\"."},{"p":"More ready-made objects","h":"Things to turn and dial","u":"more-objects.html#things-to-turn-and-dial","x":"Valve Or Wheel : turns in steps (a quarter turn by default) until fully open, then turns back. Fully open can power things (Power From State > Only When Full). On Open Amount drives gauges, water or steam. Combination Dial : a safe dial. Turn it (A / D, arrows, mouse wheel, stick) and press the interact button on each number; the right numbers in order unlock it and power the safe door."},{"p":"More ready-made objects","h":"Things to climb and sit on","u":"more-objects.html#things-to-climb-and-sit-on","x":"Ladder : grab on, climb with up / down, step off at the top or bottom exit. Turn Built In Climb off to only get the events and play your own animation. Seat : sit (placed at the seat point, facing its forward), stand with the interact button or Esc. One player per seat. Follows a moving seat (a vehicle, a swing). Both move the player's body safely (CharacterController and Rigidbody are paused meanwhile) and pause your controller through Interactor.IsBusy (or an Interaction Controller Lock)."},{"p":"More ready-made objects","h":"Things to read, hear and watch","u":"more-objects.html#things-to-read-hear-and-watch","x":"Sign : shows its text in a bubble next to it, while looked at or after using it. Audio Log : plays a clip with timed subtitles; remembers that it was heard. Screen : a monitor, TV or terminal that shows the next page (materials or objects) on each use and goes dark without power."},{"p":"More ready-made objects","h":"Things that break","u":"more-objects.html#things-that-break","x":"Breakable : hits to break (each use is one hit), or break on a hard impact, or call Damage from your weapons. It hides itself, spawns a broken version or debris, drops prefabs (Item Pickups) into the world and gives items to the breaker's inventory. Restoring its state puts it back together."},{"p":"More ready-made objects","h":"Doors in pairs and roll-up doors","u":"more-objects.html#doors-in-pairs-and-roll-up-doors","x":"Linked Parts : objects that move together, like double doors or a pair of shutters. Use either one and both open. Roll-Up Door : garage doors, shop shutters and blinds: the curtain rolls up into the top while a roller turns."},{"p":"More ready-made objects","h":"Elevators and moving platforms","u":"more-objects.html#elevators-and-moving-platforms","x":"Elevator Or Moving Platform moves between stops and carries whatever stands on it (players with a CharacterController or Rigidbody, crates). Use it to go to the next stop, call it with Elevator Call Button s on each floor, or set Automatic for a platform that goes back and forth. It stops without power. On Arrived and On Departed open and close the doors on each floor."},{"p":"More ready-made objects","h":"Rules and helpers","u":"more-objects.html#rules-and-helpers","x":"Use Limit : one time only, or a number of uses, optionally refilling after a while. Custom Condition : block the object until something happens, without code: flip it from any event, require objects to be active or inactive, or give it a check from code. Auto Reset : puts the object back by itself after a delay (doors close, levers flip back), waiting while a player is close. Camera Focus Point : moves the camera to a close-up and locks the player while using the object (a keypad, a workbench); with Cinemachine, switches on a virtual camera instead. Play Director On Use : plays a Timeline when"},{"p":"More ready-made objects","h":"Feel","u":"more-objects.html#feel","x":"Interaction Feedback : gamepad rumble, camera shake, particles and a rattle, separately for used, opened, closed and \"can't use\" (a locked handle rattles). Players can turn rumble and shake off. Interaction Sounds : several clips per sound (never the same twice in a row), random pitch and volume, and a moving sound (a creak or rumble) that gets louder and higher the faster the part moves."},{"p":"Prompts and button icons","h":"Prompts and button icons","u":"prompts.html#prompts-and-button-icons","x":"The prompt shows what the player can do (\"Open Door\") with the button for the device they used last : keyboard and mouse, Xbox, PlayStation or Switch. It changes the moment they touch a different device. When something can't be used, it shows why (\"Locked - find the red key\") in red, without a button. The prompt shows the button of the controller in use."},{"p":"Prompts and button icons","h":"Three versions","u":"prompts.html#three-versions","x":"Interaction Prompt (No Packages) : drawn with Unity's built-in GUI. Works in every project. Interaction Prompt (uGUI) : a Canvas with TextMesh Pro, for projects that use uGUI. Set Font to use your own. Interaction Prompt (Custom) : your own prompt prefab, driven by the kit (see Customizing ). The look comes from a Theme (six ready-made ones, or yours) or a Prompt Style : what it shows, layout, panel, show/hide animation, hold progress and the \"can't use\" look. Which look wins, from first to last: the object's own ( Interaction Appearance ), the prompt's Style Asset , the prompt's Theme , the p"},{"p":"Prompts and button icons","h":"Button icons (glyph sets)","u":"prompts.html#button-icons-glyph-sets","x":"The kit ships Kenney's Input Prompts icons (free, CC0) for the keyboard, mouse, Xbox, PlayStation and Switch: Runtime/Glyphs/Kenney Input Prompts.asset . Unknown controllers use the Xbox icons. A key without an icon is drawn as a key cap with its name. To use your own icons: Assets > Create > All In One Interaction Kit > Glyph Set , add a sprite per key and per gamepad button (by position: South, East, West, North...), and assign it to the prompt's Glyphs ."},{"p":"Prompts and button icons","h":"Crosshair","u":"prompts.html#crosshair","x":"Interaction Crosshair is a small dot: dim when nothing is targeted, bright when a usable object is, red when it is blocked. Colours and size are settings."},{"p":"Carry, sockets, inspect, notes and keypads","h":"Carry, sockets, inspect, notes and keypads","u":"hands-on-objects.html#carry-sockets-inspect-notes-and-keypads","x":"Objects the player handles. Make any of them with the Setup Wizard (pick the Type ) or add the component next to an Interactable."},{"p":"Carry, sockets, inspect, notes and keypads","h":"Carry and throw","u":"hands-on-objects.html#carry-and-throw","x":"Carry (needs a Rigidbody): \"Pick Up\" holds it in front of the view. It still collides with the world, so it can knock things over and be used to push buttons or weigh down plates. Use it again, or press the interact button while aiming at nothing usable, to drop it (the prompt says \"Drop ...\"). Throw : the left mouse button or the right shoulder button ( Throw Key / Throw Button ), at Throw Speed . Max Mass : heavier objects say \"Too heavy\". Only one thing at a time: \"Hands full\". Item Id (e.g. fuse ) lets an Item Socket recognise it. Events: On Picked Up, On Dropped, On Thrown."},{"p":"Carry, sockets, inspect, notes and keypads","h":"Item sockets","u":"hands-on-objects.html#item-sockets","x":"Item Socket : a place for a carried item, like a fuse box, a gem slot or a battery holder. Carry the item with the matching Accepts Item Id to it and use it: the item snaps to the Snap Point and the socket powers things (see Power and puzzles ). Without the item, the prompt says what's missing ( Missing Message , e.g. \"Needs a fuse\"). With Allow Remove , using it again hands the item back. Start Item puts one in from the start."},{"p":"Carry, sockets, inspect, notes and keypads","h":"Inspect","u":"hands-on-objects.html#inspect","x":"Inspect : brings the object up close; the mouse or right stick turns it, the interact button, Escape or the gamepad's back button puts it back where it was. Title and Description show underneath (a clue, a collectible's story). View Rotation turns it when it comes up close so its best side faces the player (X 90 for a coin or gear modelled lying flat). The player stands still meanwhile, and the prompt and crosshair hide."},{"p":"Carry, sockets, inspect, notes and keypads","h":"Readable notes","u":"hands-on-objects.html#readable-notes","x":"Readable : a note, letter or book. Its Pages show on a paper panel; A/D, the arrow keys or the shoulder buttons turn pages; the interact button or Escape closes it. Paper Color and Ink Color set the look. Has Been Read tells your code the player opened it."},{"p":"Carry, sockets, inspect, notes and keypads","h":"Keypads","u":"hands-on-objects.html#keypads","x":"Keypad : use it to open a keypad on screen and enter the Code : number keys, the mouse, or a gamepad (stick to move, the interact button to press). The right code unlocks it, which powers things : put a Power Receiver on a door and drag the keypad into its Source. Wrong codes flash \"Wrong code\"; Max Attempts in a row locks it out for Lockout Seconds . Relockable lets players lock it again. Events: On Unlocked, On Wrong Code, On Locked."},{"p":"Carry, sockets, inspect, notes and keypads","h":"In 2D games","u":"hands-on-objects.html#in-2d-games","x":"Readable notes and keypads work the same in 2D (with Proximity 2D Discovery): the panels are drawn on screen. Carry, Item Socket and Inspect are for 3D (they use 3D physics and a camera view of the object)."},{"p":"Carry, sockets, inspect, notes and keypads","h":"Your look, your text, your own UI","u":"hands-on-objects.html#your-look-your-text-your-own-ui","x":"The note, keypad and inspect panels have colour, Font , text and Close Key settings; untick Draw Panel (or Draw Text for inspect) to show your own UI instead. See Customizing ."},{"p":"Carry, sockets, inspect, notes and keypads","h":"For your own controller","u":"hands-on-objects.html#for-your-own-controller","x":"While the player inspects, reads or types a code, Interactor.IsBusy is true: stop moving and looking around (the sample controller does). Interactor.Carrying tells you what they hold."},{"p":"Carry, sockets, inspect, notes and keypads","h":"Multiplayer","u":"hands-on-objects.html#multiplayer","x":"Carry : add a Network Object, a Network Transform (Authority Mode: Owner), a Network Rigidbody and Network Carry . The player who picks it up moves it on their own machine; everyone sees it; only one player can hold it at a time. Item Socket : a Network Interactable; the host places the item, so everyone sees it in place. Keypad : a Network Interactable and Network Keypad : the host checks codes; a right code unlocks it for everyone. Inspect and Readable happen only on the player's own machine; nothing to add."},{"p":"Power and puzzles","h":"Power and puzzles","u":"power-and-puzzles.html#power-and-puzzles","x":"Wire switches, levers, buttons and pressure plates to doors, lights and anything else, with logic in between. No code. Switches, plates and logic wired to doors and lights, no code."},{"p":"Power and puzzles","h":"The idea","u":"power-and-puzzles.html#the-idea","x":"A power source is either on or off. Anything that should react to it has a field for a source: drag the GameObject with the switch (or plate, gate, puzzle) into it. In the Scene view, wires show what powers what: cyan while editing, yellow when powered and grey when off in Play mode. Tools > All In One Interaction Kit > Show Power Wires turns them on or off."},{"p":"Power and puzzles","h":"Sources","u":"power-and-puzzles.html#sources","x":"Component Powered while... Switch (on an Interactable) Toggle : it's on (\"Turn On\" / \"Turn Off\"). Momentary : for a moment after each press (\"Press\"), like a push button. Optional Moving Part that moves while on. Power From State Any part with an open/on state is on: a lever made from a Hinge , a handle made from a Slide . Added automatically with a Switch. Invert = powered while off/closed. Pressure Plate Enough weight stands on it ( Weight mode, in kg) or enough things ( Count mode). Crates count with their Rigidbody mass; players and NPCs (CharacterController or kinematic Rigidbody) as Char"},{"p":"Power and puzzles","h":"What power can do","u":"power-and-puzzles.html#what-power-can-do","x":"Component Does Power Receiver Drives a part next to it (a door's Hinge, a Slide, a Switch): Follow Power (open while powered), Open Once , Toggle On Power , or Events Only . Power opens a door even if it's locked. Needs Power (condition) The object can only be used while powered; otherwise the prompt says why (\"No power\"). Powered Light Switches Lights, and objects such as a lit bulb, with the power."},{"p":"Power and puzzles","h":"Recipes","u":"power-and-puzzles.html#recipes","x":"A lever opens a gate : make the lever with the Setup Wizard (Type Lever ), put a Power Receiver on the gate's door part, drag the lever into Source . Two plates at once : a Power Gate set to All with both plates as inputs; the door's receiver uses the gate. Press the buttons in order : three Buttons ; a Sequence Puzzle with them in the right order; a receiver on the door with Open Once . Lights out when the breaker trips : a Switch as the breaker; Powered Light on each lamp; Needs Power on the terminal."},{"p":"Power and puzzles","h":"Multiplayer","u":"power-and-puzzles.html#multiplayer","x":"Switches and levers are shared by their Network Interactable like any door. For pressure plates, gates with delays or toggles, and puzzles, add a Network Power Source : the host decides, and every player (and late joiner) gets the same value. Receivers only change doors on the host; clients receive the door's state."},{"p":"Containers and loot","h":"Containers and loot","u":"containers-and-loot.html#containers-and-loot","x":"Chests, lockers, crates and drawers that hand out items, for any inventory system. Notes, keypads and chests from The Locked Workshop."},{"p":"Containers and loot","h":"Make a container","u":"containers-and-loot.html#make-a-container","x":"Furniture or a chest with a lid or door : Setup Wizard, tick Gives loot . The first part (the lid, the door) gets a Loot Container : opening it hands out the items. A crate to search : Setup Wizard, Type Container . \"Search Crate\"; once empty it says \"Empty\". By hand : add Loot Container next to any Interactable (with or without a Hinge or Slide). Add a Lock for a locked chest."},{"p":"Containers and loot","h":"What's inside","u":"containers-and-loot.html#whats-inside","x":"Fixed Items : items that are always in this container. Table : a Loot Table (Assets > Create > All In One Interaction Kit > Loot Table) with entries: Always : always in the container, with a count between Min and Max ; otherwise one of the Random Picks , chosen by Weight (2 = twice as likely as 1). Seed : picks the random items. The same seed always gives the same loot, so every player sees the same thing. Each container gets its own seed; change it for a different result. Items are Loot Item assets (Assets > Create > All In One Interaction Kit > Loot Item): an Id for your inventory, a Display"},{"p":"Containers and loot","h":"Getting items into your inventory","u":"containers-and-loot.html#getting-items-into-your-inventory","x":"The kit has no inventory of its own. When a player opens a container, each item goes to the first component on the player that implements ILootReceiver and accepts it: public sealed class MyInventoryAdapter : MonoBehaviour, ILootReceiver { public bool TryReceive(LootItem item, int count, LootContainer from) => myInventory.TryAdd(item.Id, count); } Return false when it doesn't fit: the item stays in the container for later. Keys (items with a Key Id) go to the player's Key Ring first, so a key found in a chest opens the matching Lock . No inventory yet? The container's On Item Given event (and "},{"p":"Containers and loot","h":"Saving and multiplayer","u":"containers-and-loot.html#saving-and-multiplayer","x":"Which items were taken is part of the container's saved state (see Extending ). In multiplayer, add Network Interactable and Network Loot Delivery : the host decides who gets what, each item can be taken once, and items reach the player who opened the container on their own machine."},{"p":"Multiplayer (Netcode for GameObjects)","h":"Multiplayer (Netcode for GameObjects)","u":"multiplayer.html#multiplayer-netcode-for-gameobjects","x":"Works when your project has Netcode for GameObjects 2.0 or newer. Without it, the multiplayer parts simply don't compile and everything else works as normal. A host and a client in the multiplayer demo, and the 2D demo."},{"p":"Multiplayer (Netcode for GameObjects)","h":"How it works","u":"multiplayer.html#how-it-works","x":"The host decides every interaction: a client asks, the host checks range, locks and the rest, then applies it. The result reaches every player, and players who join later see doors and drawers exactly as they are. If the host refuses, the player who asked gets the reason (\"Locked\") in their prompt."},{"p":"Multiplayer (Netcode for GameObjects)","h":"Set up","u":"multiplayer.html#set-up","x":"On each interactive object: a Network Object (on the object or a parent) and a Network Interactable next to its Interactable . For models made with the Setup Wizard, the Interactable is on the moving part (for example door ): put the Network Interactable there and the Network Object on the prefab's root. On the player prefab: the usual Interactor , discovery and input. Only the owner's copy should read input: see Samples/Netcode/SampleNetworkPlayer.cs . Prompts follow the local player automatically when Interactor is left empty. Try Samples/Scenes/InteractionKit_DemoNetcode : click Host in one"},{"p":"Multiplayer (Netcode for GameObjects)","h":"Power and loot","u":"multiplayer.html#power-and-loot","x":"Pressure plates, gates with delays or toggles, and puzzles: add Network Power Source so every player gets the host's value. Switches and levers are already shared through Network Interactable. Loot containers: add Network Loot Delivery next to the Network Interactable. Each item can be taken once, and it is delivered on the machine of the player who opened the container. Carry, item sockets and keypads: see Carry, sockets, inspect, notes and keypads ."},{"p":"Multiplayer (Netcode for GameObjects)","h":"Good to know","u":"multiplayer.html#good-to-know","x":"Tween drives are best for networked doors: every player sees the same smooth motion. Physics doors are simulated on each machine; their open/closed state is shared. Only the durable state is sent (open or closed, locked or not, key taken), never every frame of motion."},{"p":"Customizing: make it yours","h":"Customizing: make it yours","u":"customizing.html#customizing-make-it-yours","x":"Your game shouldn't look like everyone else's. Everything the player sees can be changed or switched off: the prompt, how holding shows its progress, the \"can't use\" look, the crosshair, the panels, the sounds and the words. Start from one of six ready-made themes, change anything, give single objects their own look, or draw it all with your own UI while the kit does the work. Nothing here needs code unless it says so. The same prompt in the six ready-made themes."},{"p":"Customizing: make it yours","h":"Make it yours in a minute","u":"customizing.html#make-it-yours-in-a-minute","x":"Assets > Create > All In One Interaction Kit > Theme (Modern / Minimal / Retro / In World / High Contrast / Colourblind Safe) makes a theme asset from a ready-made look. Its inspector has the presets at the top, then the Prompt style , Crosshair style and Highlight style in foldouts. Add an Interaction Theme component to your first scene (Add Component > All In One Interaction Kit > UI) and drop your theme in. Every prompt and crosshair uses it. (No asset yet? Pick a Preset on the component.) Change anything in the theme while the game runs: the prompt and crosshair follow at once. One object "},{"p":"Customizing: make it yours","h":"Your own objects","u":"customizing.html#your-own-objects","x":"Any model or prefab: the Setup Wizard makes an interactive copy of it (doors, lids and drawers found by name, or one object as a door, switch, button, lever, plate, crate, carryable, inspectable, note, keypad or item socket). Your original is never changed. Or add an Interactable and a behaviour (Hinge, Slide, Switch...) to any GameObject yourself. Doors and drawers: open angle, hinge side and hinge point, axis, smooth (Tween: duration and easing curve) or physics motion (spring, damper, swing damping, max spin speed, free swing when idle), how far a drawer slides, in which direction and how f"},{"p":"Customizing: make it yours","h":"Your player and input","u":"customizing.html#your-player-and-input","x":"Your own controller: the kit never moves the player. Put an Interactor on it; while a note, keypad or inspected object is open, Interactor.IsBusy is true so you can pause your own controls. Finding things: Look Ray Discovery (distance, radius, Layers , triggers), Proximity Discovery and Proximity 2D Discovery (radius, Layers , facing). Only the layers you tick count. Buttons: Key Interaction Input : the keyboard key and the gamepad button. With the Input System package, Input Action Interaction Input uses any Input Action, so players can rebind it. Carry: Throw Key and Throw Button . Notes, ke"},{"p":"Customizing: make it yours","h":"The prompt","u":"customizing.html#the-prompt","x":"Every setting is on the Prompt Style (in a theme, or as its own asset on a prompt). See Prompts . What it shows: Prompt shows : Full (\"E Open Heavy Door\"), Short (just the verb, \"E Open\"), Key Only , Text Only , or None (no prompt; the crosshair and the events still work). In the style these are Content and Action Text ; one object can choose its own (Interaction Appearance > Action Text). Icon Position : left, right or above the text. Spacing , Padding , Text Case (as written, CAPITALS, lower case). Panel: on or off, Roundness (square to fully round), Outline Width and colour, a Shadow (colou"},{"p":"Customizing: make it yours","h":"The crosshair","u":"customizing.html#the-crosshair","x":"Every setting is on the Crosshair Style (in a theme, or on the crosshair). Shape: Dot , Ring , Cross , Brackets , Chevron , your own Sprite , or None ; Size , Thickness , Gap , an Outline so it reads on any background, or Show off to hide it. A look per state: Idle (looking at nothing usable), Hover (something to use), Blocked (locked, no power) and Holding : each with its own colour, size, turn, pulse, and whether it shows at all (hide it until there's something to use). Changing between looks: Transition Time and an Easing curve. Hold progress on the crosshair: a ring round it, with its own "},{"p":"Customizing: make it yours","h":"Notes, keypads and inspect","u":"customizing.html#notes-keypads-and-inspect","x":"Look: notes: Paper Color , Ink Color , Font . Keypads: Panel , Display , Digit , Wrong and Highlight colours, Font . Inspect: Text Color , Font , View Distance , View Rotation . Text: notes: Title , Pages , Pages Footer (\"Page {0} of {1} ...\"), Footer . Keypads: Wrong Code Text , Hint Text , Show Digits . Inspect: Title , Description , Hint Text . An empty hint or footer hides it. Your own UI: untick Draw Panel (notes, keypads) or Draw Text (inspect) and the kit draws nothing. Show your own UI from the On Opened / On Closed events (inspect: On Inspect Started / Ended ). Your keypad's buttons c"},{"p":"Customizing: make it yours","h":"Sounds","u":"customizing.html#sounds","x":"Add Interaction Sounds (Add Component > All In One Interaction Kit > Feedback) to an interactable object and drop your AudioClips in: Opened / Closed : when it opens or turns on, and closes or turns off (doors, drawers, lids, switches, levers, buttons). Every player hears it in multiplayer. Used : each successful use. Denied : it can't be used (locked, no power, too heavy). Keypad : Key Pressed , Code Accepted , Wrong Code . Carry : Picked Up , Dropped , Thrown . Loot : Looted (once per opening). Source (empty = a 3D Audio Source is added), Volume , Pitch Variation . Anything else can play a s"},{"p":"Customizing: make it yours","h":"Events, for sounds, effects and your own scripts","u":"customizing.html#events-for-sounds-effects-and-your-own-scripts","x":"Every object has events in the Inspector (no code) and as C# events: Interactable: On Interacted, On Denied, On Hold Started, On Hold Canceled, On State Changed. Power: every source (switch, plate, gate, puzzle, keypad, socket) has On Powered / On Unpowered; Power Receiver too; Sequence Puzzle : On Progress, On Solved, On Failed. Carry: On Picked Up, On Dropped, On Thrown. Item Socket: On Filled, On Emptied. Keypad: On Unlocked, On Wrong Code, On Locked, On Opened, On Closed, On Key Pressed. Note: On Opened, On Closed. Inspect: On Inspect Started / Ended. Loot Container: On Item Given, On Empt"},{"p":"Customizing: make it yours","h":"Your language","u":"customizing.html#your-language","x":"Every text the kit shows players (prompts, reasons such as \"Locked\", and the note, keypad and inspect text) goes through one hook. Point it at your localization system once, for example in a startup script: InteractionText.Translate = text => MyLocalization.Get(text); // return null to keep a text as written What it receives: the whole prompt as shown (\"Open Door\", \"Close Chest\"), each reason as written (\"Locked - find the red key\", \"Too heavy\"), and your own panel words (note titles and pages, inspect titles and descriptions, the panel hints and footers). So your own texts can simply be keys "},{"p":"Customizing: make it yours","h":"Loot and inventory","u":"customizing.html#loot-and-inventory","x":"Your items: Loot Item assets (id, display name, icon, key id) and Loot Table assets (always-included items, weighted random rolls, count ranges). Chests use them through Loot Container (fixed items, a table, a seed, block when empty). Your inventory: put a component that implements ILootReceiver on the player ( Containers and loot ). The sample inventory and its \"+ 7 Coin\" messages are only an example."},{"p":"Customizing: make it yours","h":"Left as they are, on purpose","u":"customizing.html#left-as-they-are-on-purpose","x":"The F3 debugger's look: a development aid, not for players (its key and whether it starts visible are settings). Power wire colours in the Scene view: editor-only (cyan while editing, yellow when powered, grey when off); they never appear in your game. Turn them off with Tools > All In One Interaction Kit > Show Power Wires . The built-in panels' layout (where the keys and the paper sit): change the colours, font and text, or untick Draw Panel and use your own UI."},{"p":"Accessibility","h":"Accessibility","u":"accessibility.html#accessibility","x":"Players set these in your options menu; every interaction in the game follows them at once. Put an Interaction Accessibility Settings component in your first scene to set them without code (turn on Remember Player Choices to keep them between sessions), or set InteractionAccessibility from your own settings menu. Setting What it does Hold To Toggle Press once to start a hold and once more to stop, instead of keeping the button down. Hold Time Scale Every hold takes longer or shorter (0.25 to 4). Mash As Hold Objects that need rapid presses ask for a hold instead. Double Tap As Press Objects th"},{"p":"Accessibility","h":"Captions","u":"accessibility.html#captions","x":"Add Interaction Captions to the scene. When the player turned captions on, every interaction sound shows a short caption (\"[opens]\", \"[locked]\"); write your own per sound on each object's Interaction Sounds (Captions list), for example \"[heavy door creaks open]\". Font, size, colours, how long they stay and how many at once are on the component; its On Caption event feeds your own subtitle UI. Audio logs show their own timed subtitles."},{"p":"Accessibility","h":"Themes for players","u":"accessibility.html#themes-for-players","x":"Two theme presets are made for accessibility: High Contrast : big bold white text on solid black, a thick yellow outline and hold ring, a large crosshair and a thick highlight outline. Colourblind Safe : the Modern look in blue and orange, colours that every common kind of colour vision can tell apart. \"Can't use\" is always written as text too (\"Locked\"), never shown by colour alone. Let players pick a theme in your options menu by setting InteractionTheme.Current ."},{"p":"Saving and integrations","h":"Saving and integrations","u":"saving-and-integrations.html#saving-and-integrations","x":""},{"p":"Saving and integrations","h":"Saving","u":"saving-and-integrations.html#saving","x":"The kit saves the state of every interactive object in the open scenes (doors open, chests looted, levers pulled, keypads unlocked, uses left, the elevator's floor) and the players' key rings. No code: add Interaction Auto Save to the scene. It loads when the scene starts and saves when the game quits (and every few seconds if you like). Call Save Now before loading another scene. Code: InteractionSave.Save(\"slot1\") and InteractionSave.Load(\"slot1\") . Saves are JSON files in Application.persistentDataPath (PlayerPrefs on WebGL). Your own save system (any asset, a cloud save): put InteractionSa"},{"p":"Saving and integrations","h":"Events for everything","u":"saving-and-integrations.html#events-for-everything","x":"Every object: Interaction State Events gives UnityEvents (no code) and a C# event for opened, closed, the state number, used and denied. Interactable.Interacted , Denied and StateChanged are C# events on every object, and Interactable.AnyInteracted fires for every object in the game. Quests, dialogue, achievements: Interaction Signal raises a named signal (\"vault_opened\") when an object is used, opened or closed. Listen with InteractionSignals.Raised (code) or an Interaction Signal Listener (no code). Start a conversation by giving a character an Interactable with a signal your dialogue system"},{"p":"Saving and integrations","h":"Visual Scripting","u":"saving-and-integrations.html#visual-scripting","x":"When the Visual Scripting package is installed, these nodes appear under Romano Assets: Use Interactable , Set Interaction State , Get Interaction State , Raise Interaction Signal , Save Or Load Interactions , and the events On Interaction Signal and On Any Interaction . The kit never requires the package."},{"p":"Saving and integrations","h":"Timeline","u":"saving-and-integrations.html#timeline","x":"When Timeline is installed, add an Interaction Track , bind an object's Interactable, and add clips that set its state (open the door during a cutscene), optionally putting the old state back when the clip ends and raising a signal. Play Director On Use plays a Timeline when an object is used (this one needs no package)."},{"p":"Saving and integrations","h":"Cinemachine","u":"saving-and-integrations.html#cinemachine","x":"Give a Camera Focus Point a Virtual Camera : a CinemachineCamera aimed at the object, switched off. During the close-up it is switched on, so Cinemachine blends to it, and switched off again after. Works with Cinemachine 2 and 3 (the kit doesn't reference the package)."},{"p":"Saving and integrations","h":"Your own character controller","u":"saving-and-integrations.html#your-own-character-controller","x":"Put an Interactor on the player, with a finder (Look Ray Discovery for first person, Proximity Discovery for third person and top-down) and an input (Key Interaction Input, or Input Action Interaction Input). Set its Origin to the camera for first person. Pause your controller while the player reads, types a code, sits or climbs: check interactor.IsBusy in your controller, or add an Interaction Controller Lock and list your controller scripts (it also frees the mouse cursor meanwhile). Optional: an Interaction Highlighter, Markers, a prompt and a crosshair (Tools > All In One Interaction Kit >"},{"p":"Saving and integrations","h":"Unity's Starter Assets","u":"saving-and-integrations.html#unitys-starter-assets","x":"Unity's free Starter Assets (first and third person) work as they are: add the Interactor to the PlayerCapsule, set its Origin to the PlayerCameraRoot (first person) or use Proximity Discovery (third person), and add an Interaction Controller Lock . It finds the Starter Assets controller by itself and pauses it while the player is busy. Use Key Interaction Input for the interact button (it reads the Input System directly), or add an \"Interact\" action to the Starter Assets input actions and use Input Action Interaction Input."},{"p":"Tools","h":"Tools","u":"tools.html#tools","x":""},{"p":"Tools","h":"Scene Overview","u":"tools.html#scene-overview","x":"Tools > All In One Interaction Kit > Scene Overview lists every interactive object in the open scenes: what it is (door, drawer, lock...), its state (live in Play mode, with its prompt), and its problems. Click a name to select the object. Only problems hides the rest; the search box filters by name or type."},{"p":"Tools","h":"Checking for problems","u":"tools.html#checking-for-problems","x":"The Scene Overview (and Tools > All In One Interaction Kit > Check Scene For Problems ) finds common setup mistakes, with a one-click fix where there is one: Problem Fix Does nothing (no part like a Hinge or Switch) Add one, or use the Setup Wizard No collider (players can't look at it) Adds a box collider around what it shows (2D for sprites) Colliders on the Ignore Raycast layer Moves them to Default Max Distance under half a metre Sets 2.5 m Empty prompt Uses the object's name No Save Id, or a Save Id used twice (copied objects) Adds one, or gives a new one No Interactor in the scene (add o"},{"p":"Tools","h":"Making many prefabs interactive","u":"tools.html#making-many-prefabs-interactive","x":"Select prefabs in the Project window (as many as you like), then Assets > All In One Interaction Kit > Make Selected Prefabs Interactive , or Convert all selected prefabs in the Setup Wizard. Models with doors, drawers and lids as child objects get each part set up; single objects are recognised by name (switch, button, lever, plate, crate, note, keypad, fuse box, door). Your originals are never changed: a new prefab is saved next to each. Anything it can't recognise is listed so you can set it up in the wizard."},{"p":"Tools","h":"Gizmos","u":"tools.html#gizmos","x":"Select an Interactable to see how close players must be (its bounds grown by Max Distance). Hinges show their arc, ladders their climb and exits, elevators their stops."},{"p":"Extending with code","h":"Extending with code","u":"extending.html#extending-with-code","x":"Everything is in the RomanoAssets.InteractionKit namespace (editor tools in RomanoAssets.InteractionKit.Editor )."},{"p":"Extending with code","h":"Events","u":"extending.html#events","x":"interactable.Interacted += (target, interactor) => Debug.Log($\"{interactor.name} used {target.name}\"); interactable.Denied += (target, interactor, check) => Debug.Log(\"Refused: \" + check.Reason); interactable.StateChanged += target => Save(); interactor.FocusChanged += (who, focus) => Highlight(focus); The same events are on the Interactable in the Inspector (On Interacted, On Denied...) for no-code use."},{"p":"Extending with code","h":"Use an object from code","u":"extending.html#use-an-object-from-code","x":"var result = interactable.Request(interactor); // the normal path (goes to the host in multiplayer) var forced = interactable.ExecuteAuthoritative(null, false); // apply now, skipping the range check (cut scenes, triggers) var check = interactable.Evaluate(interactor, true); // would it work? check.Allowed, check.Reason interactor.SetExternalInput(true); // press the interact button for AI or tests"},{"p":"Extending with code","h":"Your own behaviour","u":"extending.html#your-own-behaviour","x":"public sealed class LightSwitch : InteractionBehaviour { [SerializeField] private Light lamp; public override string Verb => lamp.enabled ? \"Turn Off\" : \"Turn On\"; public override int StateValue => lamp.enabled ? 1 : 0; public override void ApplyState(int value, bool instant) => lamp.enabled = value != 0; public override void Apply(Interactor interactor) { lamp.enabled = !lamp.enabled; NotifyStateChanged(); } } Put it next to an Interactable . StateValue / ApplyState make it save and network correctly."},{"p":"Extending with code","h":"Your own rule","u":"extending.html#your-own-rule","x":"Derive from InteractionCondition and return InteractionCheck.Allow or InteractionCheck.Block(InteractionBlocker.Condition, \"Needs power\", this) from Evaluate . The reason appears in the prompt and the debug overlay."},{"p":"Extending with code","h":"Saving and loading","u":"extending.html#saving-and-loading","x":"Each object's state is a short list of numbers: InteractableSnapshot snapshot = interactable.CaptureSnapshot(); // [Serializable]: JSON or any save system interactable.RestoreSnapshot(snapshot, instant: true);"},{"p":"Extending with code","h":"Your own input","u":"extending.html#your-own-input","x":"Derive from InteractionInputSource (the interact button, plus the key and gamepad button shown in prompts), or implement IInteractionInputBackend and call InteractionInput.SetBackend to change how keys and buttons are read."},{"p":"Extending with code","h":"Your own prompt","u":"extending.html#your-own-prompt","x":"Derive from InteractionPromptPresenter : it works out the text, button, device, fade and hold progress every frame ( View ); you only draw it."},{"p":"Upgrading","h":"Upgrading","u":"upgrading.html#upgrading","x":"How to update the kit, and what changed in each version that you may need to act on."},{"p":"Upgrading","h":"How to update","u":"upgrading.html#how-to-update","x":"Back up your project (or commit it to version control). Import the new version from the Package Manager (My Assets) over the old one. Your own prefabs, scenes and settings are not touched: the kit never edits your files, and the Setup Wizard's prefabs keep working because component names and settings are never renamed."},{"p":"Upgrading","h":"Version notes","u":"upgrading.html#version-notes","x":""},{"p":"Upgrading","h":"1.0.0","u":"upgrading.html#100","x":"First release. Nothing to do. See CHANGELOG.md for the full list of changes."},{"p":"Troubleshooting","h":"Troubleshooting","u":"troubleshooting.html#troubleshooting","x":""},{"p":"Troubleshooting","h":"Nothing happens when I press the interact key","u":"troubleshooting.html#nothing-happens-when-i-press-the-interact-key","x":"Add an Interaction Debug Overlay to the scene and press Play (F3 toggles it). It shows, for each Interactor, what it is looking at and the first rule that blocks it: Ray hit nothing / blocked by a collider : the object needs a collider, and nothing solid may sit in front of it. Too far away : raise Max Distance on the Interactable. Locked : the Interactor needs a Key Ring with the lock's key id. Nothing to do : add a behaviour (for example Hinge ) next to the Interactable. Input: … (DISABLED) : the Interactor's input action is not enabled."},{"p":"Troubleshooting","h":"The door spins around its middle","u":"troubleshooting.html#the-door-spins-around-its-middle","x":"Its pivot is in the centre of the mesh. Run Tools > All In One Interaction Kit > Setup Wizard on the prefab: it builds a copy with the hinge on the edge and leaves your original untouched."},{"p":"Troubleshooting","h":"A physics door stops part-way, or drifts open","u":"troubleshooting.html#a-physics-door-stops-part-way-or-drifts-open","x":"A Physics Hinge Drive door finishes every real push (to fully open or fully closed, in the direction it was pushed), settles back from small bumps, latches when it swings shut, and is held where it rests. If yours still stops part-way, check Finish Pushes and Free Swing When Idle are on, and that nothing solid is in the way of the full swing (a door waits while a player stands in its way, and finishes once they move). With Ignore Frame Collisions on, it ignores its own frame and the wall the frame is set into, but not other walls or furniture nearby. To make it open one way only, set Swing on "},{"p":"Troubleshooting","h":"A door opens towards the player","u":"troubleshooting.html#a-door-opens-towards-the-player","x":"Set Swing on its Hinge to Away From Player : it then opens away from whoever opens or walks into it. Furniture doors made by the wizard use Outward Only on purpose (they can't open into the cabinet)."},{"p":"Troubleshooting","h":"The wizard didn't find my drawers (or found the wrong parts)","u":"troubleshooting.html#the-wizard-didnt-find-my-drawers-or-found-the-wrong-parts","x":"Parts are found by name ( door , drawer , lid ...) or, when nothing is named like that, guessed by shape. In the wizard, change a part's Type , remove it ( x ), or click the right child in the Scene view preview and press Add part ."},{"p":"Troubleshooting","h":"3D text shows through walls","u":"troubleshooting.html#3d-text-shows-through-walls","x":"Unity's legacy 3D Text uses a shader that draws on top of everything. The demo signs use a depth-tested copy ( Samples/Art/Sample World Text.mat with the SampleWorldText component). In your game, TextMesh Pro text is depth-tested already."},{"p":"Troubleshooting","h":"\"Missing script\" on prefabs made by the wizard","u":"troubleshooting.html#missing-script-on-prefabs-made-by-the-wizard","x":"Unity's script database can go out of date after moving or renaming a project. Right-click the AllInOneInteractionKit folder, choose Reimport , then run the wizard again. The wizard refuses to save a broken prefab and tells you this."},{"p":"Troubleshooting","h":"Multiplayer: a client presses the key but the door doesn't move","u":"troubleshooting.html#multiplayer-a-client-presses-the-key-but-the-door-doesnt-move","x":"The host decides every interaction. Check the client's player object has an Interactor and the door has a Network Object and Network Interactable . If the host refuses (for example Locked ), the client gets the reason through the Interactable's Denied event."},{"p":"Troubleshooting","h":"Still stuck?","u":"troubleshooting.html#still-stuck","x":"See Support : Discord https://discord.gg/AmpBDxRAKu, bug tracker https://github.com/romanoassets/RomanoAssetSupport, website https://romanoassets.github.io. Please paste the kit's support info (kit version, Unity version, render pipeline)."},{"p":"Support","h":"Support","u":"support.html#support","x":""},{"p":"Support","h":"Where to get help","u":"support.html#where-to-get-help","x":"Discord: https://discord.gg/AmpBDxRAKu In the server's onboarding question \"Which Romano Assets kits do you use?\", pick All In One Interaction Kit . That gives you the kit's role so you see its news. Ask in #help , report problems in #bug-reports , suggest ideas in #feature-requests . Add the Interaction Kit tag to your post. Bug tracker: https://github.com/romanoassets/RomanoAssetSupport Search the open issues first: your bug may already be known. Use the Bug report form and pick this kit in its Product list (label interaction-kit ). Website: https://romanoassets.github.io Email: marklromano@ou"},{"p":"Support","h":"What to include","u":"support.html#what-to-include","x":"Paste the kit's support info into your post or issue: Kit version (Tools > All In One Interaction Kit > Help and Support > Copy Support Info gives you all of this) Unity version (exact, from Unity Hub, e.g. 6000.3.24f1) Render pipeline (Built-in, URP or HDRP) Input: legacy Input Manager or Input System (and its version) Multiplayer: Netcode for GameObjects version, and whether the problem happens on the host, a client or both What you did, what you expected, what happened, and any Console errors The in-game debug overlay ( Interaction Debug Overlay component, F3) shows why an object can't be u"},{"p":"Changelog","h":"Changelog","u":"changelog.html#changelog","x":"All notable changes to the All In One Interaction Kit. The format follows Keep a Changelog and versions follow Semantic Versioning ."},{"p":"Changelog","h":"[1.0.0] - 2026-10-29","u":"changelog.html#100---2026-10-29","x":"First release."},{"p":"Changelog","h":"Added","u":"changelog.html#added","x":"Prompt: Short text (just the verb) and Key Only; a hold ring that follows the button (rounded square round keys, circle round gamepad buttons), a Pie fill, a Key Fill that keeps the letter sharp and an underline Bar; Quick setup with a live preview at the top of the Prompt Style and Theme inspectors. Messages: every \"can't use\" reason (locked, needs an item, no power, wait, used up, in use, too far, hands full) can show as full text, short text, an icon, the icon in the needed key's colour, icon and short text, or nothing; per theme, per kind and per object. Built-in crisp icons (lock, key, po"}];
